Error: invalid workflow specification 'workflow-spec': workflow specification must be in format 'owner/repo/workflow-name[@version]'
Usage:
  trial <workflow-spec>... [flags]

Examples:
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/weekly-research                         # Run a single workflow in a temporary trial repository
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/daily-plan githubnext/agentics/weekly-research # Compare multiple workflows
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/daily-plan myorg/myrepo/custom-workflow # Run workflows from different repositories
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --host-repo myorg/myrepo    # Use an existing host repository
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --logical-repo myorg/myrepo # Simulate a different github.repository value
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --clone-repo myorg/myrepo   # Clone repository contents into the trial host
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --repeat 3                  # Run 4 times total (1 initial + 3 repeats)
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --delete-host-repo-after    # Delete the trial host repository when done
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --dry-run                   # Preview changes without executing
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --json                      # Output trial results in JSON format
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --auto-merge-prs            # Auto-merge PRs created during the trial
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --host-repo .               # Use the current repository as the host
  gh aw trial ./local-workflow.md --clone-repo upstream/repo --repeat 2   # Run a local workflow against cloned contents
  gh aw trial githubnext/agentics/my-workflow --trigger-context https://github.com/owner/repo/issues/123 # Provide issue context for issue-triggered workflows


Flags:
      --append string                   Append extra content to the end of agentic workflow on installation
      --auto-merge-prs                  Auto-merge any pull requests created during trial execution
      --clone-repo string               Clone the contents of the specified repository into the host repository before execution (useful for testing against actual repository state)
      --delete-host-repo-after          Delete the host repository after completion (kept by default)
      --dry-run                         Show what would be done without making any changes
  -e, --engine string                   Override AI engine (copilot, claude, codex, gemini, crush)
      --force-delete-host-repo-before   Force delete the host repository before creation if it already exists
  -h, --help                            help for trial
      --host-repo string                Custom host repository slug (defaults to '<username>/gh-aw-trial'). Use '.' for current repository
  -j, --json                            Output results in JSON format
  -l, --logical-repo string             Repository to simulate workflow execution against, as if the workflow was installed there (defaults to current repository)
      --no-security-scanner             Disable security scanning of workflow markdown content
      --repeat int                      Number of additional times to run after the initial execution (e.g., --repeat 3 runs 4 times total)
      --timeout int                     Execution timeout in minutes (default 30)
      --trigger-context string          Trigger context URL (e.g., GitHub issue URL) for issue-triggered workflows
  -y, --yes                             Skip confirmation prompts

